            <div xml:id="d576">

                <pb facs="0961" n="891" sameAs="frus:frus1883/pg891"/>

                <head>No. 577.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Aristarchi Bey to Mr.
                    Frelinghuysen</hi>.</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Imperial Legation of Turkey</hi>, <hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1882-11-25"><hi rendition="#italic">November</hi> 25, 1882</date>.
                        (Received November 27.)</dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Secretary of State</hi>: As you will be pleased
                    to see, on reading the dispatch herewith inclosed in copy and dated the first of
                    this month, the Sublime Porte, being desirous of affording an additional
                    guarantee to the principle of order, contemplates interdicting the passage of
                    the Straits of the Dardanelles and of the Black Sea to vessels carrying dynamite
                    or other dangerous substances.</p>
                <p>The imperial Government attaches an especial importance to this question and
                    permits itself to count upon the benevolent concurrence of the Government of the
                    United States in this relation.</p>
                <p>Be pleased to accept, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>G. D’ARISTARCHI.</signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d576-a1.xml" xpointer="d576-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
